    browser_engine_missing_ua_defaults_2026-07-11, 1, "revalidated 2026-11-02 (close-invalid lane): action=fixed_pending_verification NOT confirmed - no merged fix commit or passing regression cited in the bug doc or git history; keep open"
    browser_engine_missing_ua_defaults_2026-07-11, 990, "2026-11-09 p3-browser sweep: UA defaults confirmed present in tag_defaults (re-verify c0a0ce86b5c, ancestor); executed browser_renderer_ua_defaults_spec was 1/2 because the Draw-IR text emission used node.text_trimmed even for white-space:pre/nowrap runs whose wrap ranges index the preserved text (<pre> drew X at the left edge of a box sized for 4 leading spaces). Fixed paint_layout.spl to emit text_data for nowrap runs (both the first-line and extra-line emitters); spec 2/2 PASS on seed interpreter; h4/h5 font_size 16/13 and pre white_space_nowrap=true confirmed via debug_style probes. Adjacent finding: bold is computed (h4 bold=true) but NOT rasterized engine-wide - inline font-weight:bold gives pixel-identical ink to normal in both software and engine2d lanes; needs the font/text raster lane, separate row."
    browser_engine_missing_ua_defaults_2026-07-11, 991, "2026-11-09 follow-up (p3-bold lane): the adjacent bold-not-rasterized finding is FIXED in the software framebuffer lane. Root causes: (1) the cascade computed st.bold but the text paint pass never passed it into the rasterizer - fb_text_thin_scaled_clip_range_adv calls in simple_web_html_layout_renderer_paint_raster.spl received only st.font_style_italic, and fb_glyph_thin_scaled_clip had no weight parameter at all (italic had a synthesis path, bold had none); (2) for <b>, tag_defaults had no b/strong UA bold branch, so bold was not even computed. Fix: thread a bold flag through fb_glyph_thin_scaled_clip / fb_text_thin_scaled_clip_range / _range_adv and apply deterministic fake-bold (each inked 5x7 bitmap pixel block extended by one extra column on the right edge - no bold face exists for the bundled/generic families on Linux; browser_platform_*_bold_faces are macOS-only, recorded not synthesised per font_provider.spl policy); added the b/strong branch to tag_defaults beside the existing th/h1-h6 idiom. Evidence: new spec test/02_integration/rendering/font_weight_bold_raster_spec.spl RED normal_ink=36 bold_ink=36 (pixel-identical for both inline font-weight:bold and <b>) then GREEN 36 vs 54 (+50 percent) on the seed interpreter; neighbours PASS: browser_renderer_spec 130/130, text_align_center_spec 4/4, browser_renderer_ua_defaults_spec 2/2, paint_primitives_coverage_closure 77/77, table_row_horizontal_layout 2/2."

